# Case B — Music Studio Infrastructure

## Client and problem
- **Client:** Mr. O'Neal (music teacher, Pomfret School). Dr. Burns is a co-teacher on calendar invites.
- **Problem:** lesson materials are scattered, scheduling is manual back-and-forth, and there is no central record of each student's progress.
- **Goal:** a Music Student Profile portal (roster, inline profiles, schedules from Sheets) that grew into scheduling, Drive resources, and lesson recaps. Future ideas: automated reminders, AI tagging of sheet music, voice-transcribed lesson summaries.

## Team
- Developers: Serena Xu, JT Gannon. Club lead: Cayden Auyang. Serena's original April 2026 UI commits are on `archive/serena-continued-work`.

## Stack and architecture
- **Frontend:** Vite 6 + React 18 + TypeScript (strict, `noUnusedLocals`) + react-router 6 with **HashRouter** (GitHub Pages only serves `/404.html` at the publishing root, so deep links must live after `#`). Entry `src/main.tsx`, routes in `src/App.tsx`, pages in `src/pages/`, components in `src/components/`, API clients in `src/api/`, helpers in `src/lib/`, shared types in `src/types.ts`, styles in `src/index.css` (Pomfret palette, Crimson Pro + Inter).
- **Backend:** one Google Apps Script web app, `apps-script/Code.gs`, bound to the studio Google Sheet (tabs: `Form Responses 1`, `Lesson Schedule`, `Lesson Recaps`, one tab per student). `GET` routes by query params (`?action=list`, `?action=schedule-list`, `?email=`); `POST` routes by `action` in a `text/plain` JSON body (CORS). The endpoint list and body shapes are in the header comment of `Code.gs`; keep it in sync when adding actions.
- **Two ways the site can be served:** (1) The old secret path (GitHub Pages, `npm run dev`): every POST includes `secret` in its body and every GET includes `&secret=` in its query string, both checked against the `SHARED_SECRET` Script Property (`isValidSecret_`). Since the Oct 7 handoff its public deployment is archived and `SHARED_SECRET` / `OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` are deleted, so in production every secret-checked request is refused and `npm run dev` can't reach the live script; keep the code, and use the editor's test deployment (`/dev`) for live checks. (2) **Google hosting** (Pomfret sign-in; the live site, Mr. O'Neal's deployment, see `docs/handoff.md`): `npm run build:gas` builds one self-contained `dist-gas/Index.html` (no `VITE_*` values in it), pasted as the editor's HTML file `Index`; `doGet` with no params serves it to `ALLOWED_USERS`, and the page calls `api(request)` through `google.script.run`, which checks `Session.getActiveUser()` against `ALLOWED_USERS` on every call and runs the same code as the GET routes (`readRoute_`) and `doPost` (`runPostAction_`). In `src/api/`, every request goes through `callAppsScript` in `appsScriptTransport.ts`, which picks the path.
- **Safety rule (same as Case A):** a page served by Apps Script can call any top-level function whose name doesn't end in `_`. Every function in `Code.gs` ends in `_` except `doGet`, `doPost`, `api`, `authorize`, `setupSheetFormatting` (editor-only via `requireEditorRun_`) and `onFormSubmit` (real trigger events only). A test enforces this; never add a public function without a caller check.
- **Config:** `.env.local` → `VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_BASE_URL`, `VITE_APPS_SCRIPT_SHARED_SECRET` (typed in `src/vite-env.d.ts`). Apps Script Script Properties: `MUSIC_STUDIO_SPREADSHEET_ID`, `CLASS_RESOURCES_FOLDER_ID`, `STUDENT_RESOURCES_PARENT_FOLDER_ID`, cached `STUDENT_FOLDER:<email>` ids, `ALLOWED_USERS` (Pomfret emails allowed on the Google-hosted site), `TIMESHEET_SPREADSHEET_ID` (ID or full URL of the payroll time sheet: Mr. O'Neal's own copy since the handoff), `TIMESHEET_START_DATE` (yyyy-MM-dd; earlier lessons are never offered), saved `TIMESHEET_STUDENT:<email>` spellings (JSON), and `SHARED_SECRET` only for the old secret path (deleted in production). Never commit their values, and never commit a spreadsheet link: the site gets the Lesson Schedule and time sheet links at runtime from `studio-links`.
- **Deploy:** the live site is Mr. O'Neal's Pomfret-only Apps Script deployment, running as him. Only he deploys (Deploy → Manage deployments → ✏️ → New version); a deploy from another account would make it run as that account, and it must never be archived. Code.gs and `Index` are pasted with `scripts/copy-to-apps-script.sh code|page`. GitHub Pages (`.github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml`) only publishes a "moved" page; `vite.config.ts` `base` must still equal `/<repo-name>/` for `npm run build`.

## Phases shipped (see README for setup of each)
1. Roster + inline profiles from Sheets. 2. Calendar event creation (`preview-event`, `create-event`, `cancel-event`; writes `Calendar Event ID`, flips Status to `Scheduled`). 3. Class Resources shared Drive folder (viewer access sync). 4. Per-student Drive folders with editor access. 5. Teacher lesson recaps (`Lesson Recaps` tab, composite key student email + lesson date + start time, drafts in localStorage). 6. Payroll time sheet (`timesheet-status`, `preview-timesheet-row`, `add-timesheet-row`, `skip-timesheet-row`; writes A-G only, into the row below the last row with anything in A-G (pre-made rows holding only an unticked checkbox count as empty), copying the format and dropdowns of the lesson row above; never H/I/J, never CHAPEL or lookup tabs; over 45 minutes = 1.5 hours and `Double`; term label rows only on tabs that already have one; remembers each student's spelling; marks the Lesson Schedule's auto-managed `Time Sheet` column, e.g. `Added 10/7/2026 (70 min, logged as 1.5)`; Dashboard "Time sheet" card). Post-delivery: warning-only Lesson Schedule dropdowns (Student Email, Student Name, Lesson Block; set by `setupSheetFormatting`, refreshed by `onFormSubmit`) and `studio-links` for the header's Lesson Schedule and Time sheet links.

## Constraints
- The script never lowers a Drive permission and never deletes a folder; keep that invariant.
- Any change to `Code.gs` needs a **new deployment version**, clicked by Mr. O'Neal only; remind the developer. Bump `CODE_VERSION` near the top of `Code.gs`; `scripts/copy-to-apps-script.sh` copies it for pasting.
- The time sheet is payroll data: write only columns A-G of new rows, never H, I or J (never tick the COMPLETED LESSON box), never edit or delete its rows, never touch its CHAPEL/MISC. or lookup tabs.
- `npm test` (node:test + node:vm, fakes in `tests/helpers/`) runs `Code.gs` against made-up data, compares every GET route with `tests/fixtures/get-routes-golden.json`, and builds the Google page; it, `npm run build` and `npm run build:gas` must pass before pushing. `scripts/copy-to-apps-script.sh code|page` copies Code.gs or the built page for pasting.
- New env vars go in `.env.example` (placeholder + comment), `src/vite-env.d.ts`, the README table, and both workflows.
- `npm run build` runs `tsc --noEmit` first; unused variables fail the build.
- Do not commit `dist/`, `node_modules/`, or `.env.local`.
